## Interim assumptions, anchored to international evidence {#interim-assumptions-anchored-to-international-evidence}

These were previously flagged as `[Evidence gap]`. None of them is a genuine SA epistemic gap — each is either an administrative number DALRRD can produce, or a value defensibly anchored to published international evidence. The Parameter Playground exposes each as an editable input.

| Item | Status | International anchor | SA working value | Sensitivity range |
|:-----|:-------|:---------------------|:-----------------|:------------------|
| Terbufos attributable fraction of fatal cases | Bracketed | Sri Lanka single-agent Class Ia withdrawals: 20–40 %[^gunnell] | **25 %** | 20–35 % |
| Maize yield impact of full withdrawal | Bracketed | EU 2009 phase-out: no documented yield collapse; SA maize ~85 % Bt-trait already covers stalk-borer use case | **<5 %**, concentrated in non-Bt smallholder maize | 0–7 % |
| Substitute acute-hazard profile | Settled | WHO classification: chlorantraniliprole (U, LD50 >5,000), thiamethoxam (II, 1,563), imidacloprid (II, 450) vs terbufos (Ia, 1.6–4.5)[^who] | Substitutes are 100–1,000× less acutely toxic on rat oral LD50 — acute-poisoning burden retired is essentially the full terbufos attributable share | n/a |
| Substitute pricing delta | Bracketed | International benchmark: substitutes 2–5× per-ha cost of commodity granular OPs | **3× input cost**, ~single-digit % of gross output at R20k/ha | 2–5× |
| SA market volume of terbufos | Administrative | n/a | **To be supplied by DALRRD** within 3 months from register + SARS HS-code customs data + CropLife SA sales returns | n/a |
| Compiled NICD/NHLS/forensic case series 2020–present | Administrative | n/a | **Compilation task, not new research**; Davies 2023 already covers paediatric subset | n/a |
| DALRRD RUP-enforcement cost | Administrative | US EPA RUP enforcement cost / inspector scaled to SA inspectorate headcount | **~R1–3M/yr** | R0.5–5M/yr |

